  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-04T02:43:43.768Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat needs arrow key movement support. It's just ridiculous at this point that WASD is the only way to move still. I mean sure, it's an easy mod to do, but that's bannable even though it wouldn't negatively impact anyone. Key bindings are literally in Unity beginner tutorials and VRChat, after 4 years, doesn't even have that. My right hand has cerebral palsy and can't use a mouse and it is VERY bothersome to have to reposition my keyboard for VRChat every time. VRChat even ignores the bindings in the config window when starting it with the shift key held",
